 "title": "Properties of the common modification, [stacks-project]",
 "statement": "Each constructed map $X'_i\\to X_i$ is a $U$-admissible blow-up. Each\n$X'_i\\to\\mathsf{CM}(X_1,X_2;U)$ is an open immersion, their two copies of\n$U$ agree, and $\\mathsf{CM}(X_1,X_2;U)$ is separated and of finite type\nover $S$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-common/lemma-nagata-common-modification.md",
